From 2bf6fd173293612066b2079c2b34cd59302e362b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:50:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] aarch64_ilp32: drop the time32 and stat64 system call numbers

The ILP32 kernel ABI keeps the time32 system calls of the AArch32 ABI
and the stat64 calls with the ARM struct stat64. Their types do not
match the 64-bit time_t of this port, so, as for riscv32,
bits/syscall.h no longer names them and musl uses only the time64
calls and statx: kstat.h is empty and __NR_futex is __NR_futex_time64.
The ILP32 kernel uapi hides the same numbers.

settimeofday_time32 stays, under its arm name, for callers that set
only the timezone: busybox hwclock uses SYS_settimeofday_time32 when
SYS_settimeofday is missing.
---
 arch/aarch64_ilp32/bits/syscall.h.in | 30 ++--------------------------
 arch/aarch64_ilp32/kstat.h           | 22 --------------------
 arch/aarch64_ilp32/syscall_arch.h    |  8 ++++++++
 3 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 50 deletions(-)

